s and can be investigated using biochemical measurements (e.g., blood tests) [Data: Entities (92, 125); Relationships (120, 141)].\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"rating\": 4.5,\n  \"rating_explanation\": \"Impact is moderate because the community describes core body-wide regulatory mechanisms and clinically relevant dysfunction pathways (e.g., hormone-driven blood sugar changes and functioning tumors), but it does not describe intentional harmful activity by agents.\"\n}", "role": "assistant", "tool_calls": null, "function_call": null}, "provider_specific_fields": {"native_finish_reason": "stop"}}], "usage": {"completion_tokens": 1742, "prompt_tokens": 3248, "total_tokens": 4990, "completion_tokens_details": {"accepted_prediction_tokens": null, "audio_tokens": null, "reasoning_tokens": 137, "rejected_prediction_tokens": null, "text_tokens": null}, "prompt_tokens_details": {"audio_tokens": null, "cached_tokens": 0, "text_tokens": null, "image_tokens": null}}, "service_tier": null}}}